 failing all; तोय˚, अन्न˚, आहार˚ &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Annihilation, death, destruction; (वचो...पथ्यमुक्तम्) राक्षसानामभावाय त्वं वा न प्रतिपद्यसे Rām.5.21.1. non-entity; नाभाव उपलब्धेः Ś B.; क्षणमात्रभवामभावकाले Śi.2.64; Ki.18.1.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(In phil.) Privation, non-existence, nullity or negation, supposed to be the seventh category or पदार्थ in the system of Kaṇāda. (Strictly speaking अभाव is not a separate predicament, like द्रव्य, गुण, but is only a negative arrangement of those predicaments; all nameable things being divided into positive (भाव) and negative (अभाव), the first division including द्रव्य, गुण, कर्म, सामान्य, विशेष and समवाय; and the second only one अभाव; cf. अत्र सप्तमस्याभावकथनादेव षण्णां भावत्वं प्राप्तं तेन भावत्वेन पृथगुपन्यासो न कृतः Muktā.) अभाव is defined as भावभिन्नो$भावः (प्रतियोगिज्ञानाधीनविषयत्वम्) that whose knowledge is dependent on the knowledge of its प्रतियोगी. It is of two principal kinds संसर्गाभाव and अन्योन्याभाव; the first comprising three varieties प्रागभाव, प्रध्वंसाभाव, and अत्यन्ताभाव. -Comp. -संपत्तिः f. false attribution (= अध्यास q. v.)", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["abhaava", "abhāva"], "synonyms_slp1": ["abhaava", "abhāva"]}], "aBavana": [{"id": "aBAvanA", "headword": "अभावना", "headword_slp1": "aBAvanA", "fold": "aBavana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "अभावना [abhāvanā], 1 Absence of judgement or right discernment.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "Absence of religious meditation.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["abhaavanaa", "abhāvanā"], "synonyms_slp1": ["abhaavanaa", "abhāvanā"]}], "aBavaniya": [{"id": "aBAvanIya", "headword": "अभावनीय", "headword_slp1": "aBAvanIya", "fold": "aBavaniya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "अभावनीय [abhāvanīya], a. Inconceivable.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["abhaavaniiya", "abhāvanīya"], "synonyms_slp1": ["abhaavaniiya", "abhāv